Why This Is Asked
Assess the ability to reason with Kleene 3-valued semantics in a constrained CSP and to design a propagation/backtracking approach that handles unknowns.

Key Concepts
- Kleene 3-valued logic: T>U>F; ¬T=F, ¬F=T, ¬U=U; ∧/∨ use min/max under T>U>F; A→B := ¬A ∨ B.
- Constraint propagation in a small CSP with unknowns; existence of a model containing U.
- Backtracking strategies to prune non-viable branches.

Code Example
```javascript
const V = {T:'T', F:'F', U:'U'}
functionNot(x){ if (x==='T') return 'F'; if (x==='F') return 'T'; return 'U' }
function kleeneOr(a,b){ if (a==='T' || b==='T') return 'T'; if (a==='U' || b==='U') return 'U'; return 'F' }
function kleeneAnd(a,b){ if (a==='F' || b==='F') return 'F'; if (a==='U' || b==='U') return 'U'; return 'T' }
function implies(a,b){ return kleeneOr(functionNot(a), b) }
```

